[step] Specific positive body-stop interface: four flat 4 × 12 mm lands stand 0.250 mm fore of the fixed wall, ending exactly at the lower cartridge aft plane Y82.265. Their 48 mm² faces establish the cartridge pose and carry both insertion reaction and seating moments independently of magnet faces and TPU tip stops. body-stop-native-review.json reads all four actual final bearing faces, 3 mm integral root stock, positive overtravel reaction and cartridge/cap withdrawal.
alternatives: Making the land flush leaves the cartridge without its positive stop across the required 0.250 mm body air. Advancing the whole wall to the bearing plane removes that running clearance through the cap and fluid interfaces. A separate shim or adjustable screw adds factory parts and another seating datum. The localized flat lands preserve the named lower-cradle contact planes.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
click: x=-100.000 y=82.265 z=223.925

[step] Required SB443-IN groove-capture interface: the rail projects 0.700 mm into the 6.650 mm slot and is 0.600 mm along Y. The supplier full-tolerance common groove is only 0.8382 mm wide (1.8542–2.6924 behind the bare pole); the rail occupies 2.000–2.600 mm, and its tips leave 0.1104 mm against the largest groove neck. Mechanically keyed DP420 bedding fills the actual axial groove allowance. magnet-geometry.json binds complete supplier loading, bare-face position and positive keyed capture in this actual exported host. Printed rail/key strength and repeated removal remain unqualified.
alternatives: A 3 mm rail cannot enter this purchased groove. Extending it along Y consumes the recorded supplier groove clearance; increasing its X projection consumes the worst-neck air. Removing it leaves adhesion as the axial restraint. A different magnet or separate bolted retainer changes the purchased interface or adds factory parts and operations.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
