[sliver] Specific mating guard recess: these 1.350 mm strips are the axial depth of its four cavity boundary faces, from Y82.515 to Y83.865. They admit the moving 1.350 mm projecting guard with 0.250 mm running air while leaving the pole 0.650 mm ahead of that guard. The closed recess end to the side-key front at Y86.865 retains the complete 3.000 mm fixed housing section; the narrow face width is the required engagement depth, not a 1.350 mm wall specification. The actual host/loading/swept-guard record is magnet-geometry.json.
alternatives: A shallower recess stops the guard before the four body lands seat and before the poles meet. A deeper recess consumes the 3 mm housing before the cured side keys; widening it changes the retained radial guidance. Removing the moving guard exposes more magnet edge and changes its insertion protection. The specified recess retains this mating envelope, with physical fit and chipping qualification still open.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
