[sliver] Specific mating-stop perimeter: the 0.250 mm strip is the exposed fore projection of each 4 × 12 mm body-stop face across the cartridge/wall running gap. The current native review measures the complete 48 mm² reaction face and 3 mm root behind the wall at each station; 0.250 mm is the required stop offset, not a membrane thickness. These edges finish the four explicit lower-cradle seating planes.
alternatives: Removing the projection loses positive seating across the body air. Enlarging its Y projection changes the closing pose and both magnet/contact datums. Extending the wall across the whole gap removes required cap/fluid clearance. A perimeter bevel changes the stated full rectangular contact area; it does not provide a thicker through-wall section.
