[ledge] Specific mating-stop lower end: each 1.00 mm² horizontal face closes the 0.250 mm fore projection of a 4 × 12 mm flat reaction land. Its depth is fixed by the required cartridge/wall running gap and its fore edge by the lower-cradle seating plane. The full 48 mm² stop faces and 3 mm roots are measured in body-stop-native-review.json. Tree (auto)/Default support can approach through the empty bay before the cartridge is fitted; removal quality remains unqualified.
alternatives: Bevelling through the fore edge reduces the full rectangular reaction face and changes its lower edge. Filling below that face extends the stop into a different cradle contact region. Removing the projection loses seating across the 0.250 mm air; advancing the entire wall removes the running clearance. Keep the four bounded flat contact lands.
