[ceiling] Required flat loading/key closure above each SB443-IN stack. The full supplier block loads through the front mouth and descends along the rails; the Z202.8554 roof closes the cured fill’s upward escape path. Three millimetres of roof stock remain above that loading envelope. The rear-frame insert axes at Z208.674 need their own 3 mm surrounding stock; the overlapping pilot starts at Y89.115, within the loading cavity’s aft extent. Empty mouths open toward −Y for Tree (auto)/Default support removal before magnets and bedding are installed. Geometric access does not establish removal effort or printed finish.
alternatives: A ramp into the present mouth obstructs the full drawing loading envelope. Raising a full-width 45° roof over the 9.85 mm keyed span adds 4.925 mm at its crest, taking it to Z207.7804 and into the rear-frame pilot’s lower envelope at Z206.674. Opening the roof removes the fill’s positive-Z closure. Moving the frame locks changes the frame/receiver mounting interface. The flat closure preserves both fitted envelopes.
