[ceiling] Specific moving-guard guide crown: the Z206.1054 flat is 0.250 mm above the complete moving guard’s top at Z205.8554. The 1.350 mm-deep receiving recess keeps the same running allowance along insertion while the moving pole remains 0.650 mm ahead of its guard. magnet-geometry.json binds the actual host, complete swept guard and bare-face seating. The empty mouth is open toward −Y for Tree (auto)/Default support removal before installation; finish and cleanup remain unqualified.
alternatives: A ramp below this plane enters the moving guard’s swept envelope. Raising the crown into a ramp enlarges the designed running/tilt clearance toward the exposed magnet edges. Removing the guide crown gives up that upper guidance; changing both guard and recess changes the mating interface. Keep the uniform guide clearance and support its open crown.
