[sliver] Required purchased-body / insert-loading depth transition. These 0.850 mm face strips join the 4.30 mm-high body/ear stadium and the 2.60 mm-high knurl-loading stadium, each with the separate supported-face allowance, at body-cavity end Y86.790. The source retains 3.10 mm axial root allowance between body depth 4.15 and heat-set anchor 7.25. Exact native rejection witnesses show that extending the body cavity to the anchor removes both 3.10 mm material lines and opens cavity points only 1.427773 mm from the nominal Ø2.3 knurls, below the specified 3 mm root. The strip width is not a 0.850 mm through-wall allowance. Printed loading and screw retention remain separately unqualified.
alternatives: A straight 45-degree reconciliation of the 0.85 mm profile-height change requires 0.85 mm additional axial run, leaving 2.25 mm to anchor 7.25; the current 3.10 mm stack has only 0.10 mm beyond its 3 mm minimum. Extending the complete body-height cavity loses the quantified root. Enlarging the loading aperture through the full ear width spends the ear bearing at depth 3.00. Moving inserts deeper changes the 8 mm screw stack and loading-tool access.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
click: x=-6.442 y=86.790 z=277.499
click: x=6.442 y=86.790 z=277.499

[ceiling] Purchased connector body/ear seat roof. This closed ceiling follows the complete body envelope with slip and the separate supported-face allowance. The ear bearing remains at depth 3.00, the body cavity at depth 4.15 and the insert anchor at depth 7.25. Tree(auto)/Default support reaches it from the empty contact opening before hardware installation. Printed cleanup, fit and retention are unqualified; accessible support alone does not establish removal effort.
alternatives: Sloping down into the source stadium consumes the purchased body clearance. A one-direction 45-degree rise over the 4.15 mm body depth consumes 4.15 of the current 6.75 mm to the crown, leaving 2.60 mm rather than the nominal 3 mm. A two-sided pitched relief could limit the rise to about 2.075 mm but would change the complete body-capture, insert-loading and adjoining lead-bore profiles; that alternative has not received an exact native or print review. Removing the roof opens the body seat through the retained crown.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
click: x=0.000 y=84.653 z=277.924

[step] Required recessed fold-through TPU front lip. This Ø14.30 by 0.60 mm counterbore contains the receiver's Ø14.00 by 0.60 mm flexible lip flush within the permanent wall. Its Y83.115 floor and wall fore Y82.515 are separate fit planes. The next collar ramp starts 3 mm behind the floor, retaining the nominal rigid wall neck.
alternatives: Removing the recess puts the lip 0.60 mm in front of the wall, exceeding the seated cartridge's 0.25 mm gap by 0.35 mm where the moving dry passage is only Ø7.75. Deepening the recess reduces the 3 mm neck before the collar ramp. Extending the larger bore through the wall changes cuff confinement and X/Z location.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
