[thin] Wrong material-thickness classification across a concave corner: front-top's upper Y-stack knuckle face (|X|104.25, exposed aft of Y200, top on the frame datum Z299.65) meets the funnel-frame foot's running clearance (|X|103.75, floor Z299.65, ending on the rear-narrowing plane Y200) only at one shared edge. Between |X|103.75 and 104.25 three of the four quadrants about that edge are solid. A ray along the knuckle sample's inward normal crosses 12.75 mm of material, and from the clearance wall 3.74 mm, the flank beside the clearance (probe on the current STL).
alternatives: The reader should not rank a closest point that lies on the edge where the opposite face ends. Moving either face off the shared frame datum adds a 0.25 mm step between fitted faces.
